MediaStore: never wait on a host folder that does not answer a listing

The MediaStore sync walks the Mac folders mapped into the volume (Pictures,
Movies). opendir() on a privacy-protected media library (~/Movies/TV, the TV
app's) waits indefinitely, so the sync -- and every query behind it -- never
returned: Instagram's gallery probes the provider (an is_favorite query) before
listing, got no answer, and showed an empty gallery.
- Known protected libraries (~/Movies/TV, ~/Music/Music, ~/Music/iTunes) are
  skipped by path.
- Every host folder is listed on a helper thread with a deadline
  (MACAPK_MEDIA_LIST_TIMEOUT_MS, 1500 ms); a folder that misses it is skipped for
  the session and logged.
- ContentResolver logs a query with no provider and a provider's exception (once
  per authority/type) instead of letting them vanish inside the app;
  MACAPK_THUMB_TRACE=1 logs generated thumbnails.

